                        "entry_id": "6e690c2c-4706-3056-8613-1e45eef27b1d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One of the filaments on the inner surface of the gastric cavity of certain jellyfishes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0def095c-79be-405b-9276-57c30a67a025",
                                "sense_id": "72ad956a-c91d-3925-9af8-1740935f43fd",
                                "text": "Closer inspection, however, shows that the two phacelli of each pair originate as diverging limbs, from a simple interradial phacellus deep in the bottom of the basal stomach."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7747005a-8e0b-49cb-96bb-6c4033ec7393",
                                "sense_id": "72ad956a-c91d-3925-9af8-1740935f43fd",
                                "text": "[...] phacelli are well developed, occupying the interradial sides of the octagonal stomach cavity. Each phacellus consists of from eight to twelve brush-like filaments."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "426bd9fc-a241-4298-8b91-cb554ca83efe",
                                "sense_id": "72ad956a-c91d-3925-9af8-1740935f43fd",
                                "text": "... the phacellus placed on it, which is formed by a bow-shaped series of gastral filaments."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
